{
  "an1.306:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 1.306–315 ",
  "an1.306:0.2": "Chapter Two ",
  "an1.306:1.0": "306 ",
  "an1.306:1.1": "“Mendicants, I do not see a single thing that gives rise to unskillful qualities, or, when they have arisen, makes them increase and grow like wrong view. ",
  "an1.306:1.2": "When you have wrong view, unskillful qualities arise or, when they have arisen, they increase and grow.” ",
  "an1.307:1.0": "307 ",
  "an1.307:1.1": "“Mendicants, I do not see a single thing that gives rise to skillful qualities, or, when they have arisen, makes them increase and grow like right view. ",
  "an1.307:1.2": "When you have right view, unarisen skillful qualities arise or, when they have arisen, they increase and grow.” ",
  "an1.308:1.0": "308 ",
  "an1.308:1.1": "“Mendicants, I do not see a single thing that gives rise to unskillful qualities, or makes skillful qualities decline like wrong view. ",
  "an1.308:1.2": "When you have wrong view, unskillful qualities arise and skillful qualities decline.” ",
  "an1.309:1.0": "309 ",
  "an1.309:1.1": "“Mendicants, I do not see a single thing that gives rise to skillful qualities, or makes unskillful qualities decline like right view. ",
  "an1.309:1.2": "When you have right view, skillful qualities arise and unskillful qualities decline.” ",
  "an1.310:1.0": "310 ",
  "an1.310:1.1": "“Mendicants, I do not see a single thing that gives rise to wrong view, and once arisen, makes it grow like irrational application of mind. ",
  "an1.31